<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-015>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-015" ;
  triage:title "Seven infallible Result-wrapped functions flagged by clippy::unnecessary_wraps (not in this workspace's -D warnings lint gate)" ;
  triage:description "rust-qa-agent's phase-end review (AT-PHASECLOSE-QA-R2, PR #1065) ran `cargo clippy -- -W clippy::unnecessary_wraps` (a lint not enabled in this workspace's default/-D-warnings gate) and found seven functions whose Result return type has no fallible code path, all returning unconditional Ok(...): crates/atm-core/src/write/acknowledgement.rs:367 finish(), crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/analyst_query.rs:422 advance_nested_sql_state(), crates/atm-core/src/mailbox/atomic.rs:85 identity(), crates/atm-core/src/mailbox/store.rs:60 identity() (near-duplicate of atomic.rs:85), crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/owner_gate.rs:128 sync_owner_record_shadow(), crates/atm/src/composition.rs:62 install_local_runtime_for_read_only_command(), crates/atm-daemon/src/bin_support/daemon_observability.rs:850 retained_sink_fault_mode(). None fail any requested check (fmt/clippy/tests/coverage/artifacts all pass); reported per an explicit dispatch checklist item, not a merge gate. Route to rust-best-practices-agent to judge which are genuinely infallible cleanup candidates versus deliberate forward-compatible API shapes before any code change." ;
